KG42.register("rules-27af3a3a702705f97a98425b",{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R003","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market clearing","process_stage":"clearing","market_meaning":"Submitted demand bids provide inputs to local market clearing. Scope: Supply-and-demand inputs to the local multi-energy-carrier auction. The requested quantity submitted in a demand bid limits the quantity cleared from that bid: clearing cannot exceed its bid quantity. Scope: The cleared quantity of each demand bid in the local auction. Submitted supply bids provide inputs to local market clearing. Scope: Supply-and-demand inputs to the local multi-energy-carrier auction. The offered quantity submitted in a supply bid limits the quantity cleared from that bid: clearing cannot exceed its bid quantity. Scope: The cleared quantity of each supply bid in the local auction. The solution of the consumer-and-producer-surplus optimization determines which bids are accepted or rejected in local clearing. Scope: Allocation decisions produced by the local market's surplus-maximizing optimization. The local market operator operates the clearing function. Scope: Operation of the local market clearing function. Receipt of demand submissions forms part of the joint all-bids-received condition under which the operator clears the local market. Scope: The centralized two-sided auction's joint all-bids receipt condition. Condition: All bids for the auction have been received, encompassing both supply and demand submissions. Receipt of supply submissions forms part of the joint all-bids-received condition under which the operator clears the local market. Scope: The centralized two-sided auction's joint all-bids receipt condition. Condition: All bids for the auction have been received, encompassing both supply and demand submissions. The design clears multiple energy carriers simultaneously through one common optimization. Scope: Common local clearing of multiple energy carriers. The market is cleared once per hour, shortly before each delivery-hour begins. Scope: The paper's rolling-horizon implementation with one-hour delivery periods. Condition: The time-period length is assumed to be 1 h. Each clearing returns results for the full trading horizon. Results for the upcoming binding hour are final, while results for subsequent advisory hours are updated in later clearings. Scope: Allocation results across the rolling trading horizon. Centralized local clearing decides how to dispatch these assets optimally. Scope: Assets whose flexibility is represented using the model's bid-dependency instruments. Condition: Agents apply bid dependencies to provide asset flexibility to the market. Partial clearing of bids is permitted. Scope: Acceptance of bids in the proposed local market. The amount cleared from a bid must be nonnegative. Scope: The cleared amount of every bid. Net energy injection must equal net outflow at each pricing location, ensuring that total supply equals total demand for each time-period and energy carrier. Scope: Each pricing location, time-period and energy carrier in local clearing. Clearing must respect network transfer limitations so that accepted bid combinations do not produce flows beyond local distribution-network capabilities; transfers between adjacent pricing locations are bounded by transfer capacity. Scope: Network-constrained allocations between carrier-specific pricing locations within the local market. The same proportion of every bid in the dependency must clear. Scope: Local clearing of bids in the same AND-dependency. Condition: Bids are included in an AND-dependency. The total accepted quantity from the dependency's bids must not exceed the specified amount. Scope: Local clearing of bids in an LE-dependency. Condition: The dependency type is LE. The total accepted quantity from the dependency's bids must be at least the specified amount. Scope: Local clearing of bids in a GE-dependency. Condition: The dependency type is GE. The total accepted quantity from the dependency's bids must equal the specified amount. Scope: Local clearing of bids in an EQ-dependency. Condition: The dependency type is EQ. The sum of the cleared fractions of the dependency's bids must not exceed one. Scope: Local clearing of bids in the same OR-dependency, including partial acceptance. Condition: Bids are included in an OR-dependency. An individual out-of-the-money bid may be accepted only with compensating bids that make its dependency collectively in-the-money. Scope: Acceptance of individual bids connected by AND-dependencies or OR-dependencies. Condition: An individual bid is out-of-the-money and other bids in its dependency compensate for it so that the dependency altogether is in-the-money. No bids in the OR-dependency clear when the dependency as a whole is unprofitable. Scope: The implemented inequality formulation of an OR-dependency. Condition: The bid dependency as a whole is unprofitable. The proportion of district heat supplied from low-temperature sources must be restricted to ensure that the water reaches a sufficiently high temperature. Scope: District-heating allocations involving low-temperature heat sources. Condition: Heat sources deliver below the target temperature of the district-heating system.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function clearing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","clearing.local","clearing.social_welfare","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"clearing.local","type":"limits","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E001","v141-b-g01-E024"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E002","source":"bidding.demand","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E022"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E003","source":"bidding.supply","target":"clearing.local","type":"limits","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E001","v141-b-g01-E024"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E004","source":"bidding.supply","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E022"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E005","source":"clearing.local","target":"bidding.demand","type":"conditional_on","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E006","source":"clearing.local","target":"bidding.supply","type":"conditional_on","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E007","source":"clearing.social_welfare","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E040"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E008","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Acceptance of bids in the proposed local market. | Acceptance of individual bids connected by AND-dependencies or OR-dependencies. | Allocation decisions produced by the local market's surplus-maximizing optimization. | Allocation results across the rolling trading horizon. | Assets whose flexibility is represented using the model's bid-dependency instruments. | Common local clearing of multiple energy carriers. | District-heating allocations involving low-temperature heat sources. | Each pricing location, time-period and energy carrier in local clearing. | Local clearing of bids in a GE-dependency. | Local clearing of bids in an EQ-dependency. | Local clearing of bids in an LE-dependency. | Local clearing of bids in the same AND-dependency. | Local clearing of bids in the same OR-dependency, including partial acceptance. | Network-constrained allocations between carrier-specific pricing locations within the local market. | Operation of the local market clearing function. | Supply-and-demand inputs to the local multi-energy-carrier auction. | The centralized two-sided auction's joint all-bids receipt condition. | The cleared amount of every bid. | The cleared quantity of each demand bid in the local auction. | The cleared quantity of each supply bid in the local auction. | The implemented inequality formulation of an OR-dependency. | The paper's rolling-horizon implementation with one-hour delivery periods.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E001","v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E018","v141-b-g01-E019","v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E024","v141-b-g01-E025","v141-b-g01-E029","v141-b-g01-E030","v141-b-g01-E035","v141-b-g01-E036","v141-b-g01-E037","v141-b-g01-E040","v141-b-g01-E043","v141-b-g02-E24","v141-b-g03-E01"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-X001","symbol":"y_b","meaning":"Amount cleared from bid b, in kWh; shorthand for y_{b,t,e,l} when time, energy-carrier and pricing-location indices are not needed. It is the optimization variable of the local clearing.","kind":"operational","domain":"Real-valued; 0 ≤ y_b ≤ q_b for every bid b ∈ B (Eq. 2)","unit":"kWh","indices":["b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E024"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-X002","symbol":"inj_{t,e,l}","meaning":"Net energy injection at pricing location l for time-period t and energy carrier e, defined in Eq. (8) from cleared supply and demand bids.","kind":"operational","domain":"Real-valued auxiliary clearing quantity at each time-period, energy carrier and pricing location","unit":"kW","indices":["t","e","l"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E032","v141-b-g01-E036"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-X003","symbol":"flo_{t,e,l}","meaning":"Net energy outflow from pricing location l for time-period t and energy carrier e, defined in Eq. (9) from angle differences and admittance across adjacent locations.","kind":"operational","domain":"Real-valued auxiliary clearing quantity at each time-period, energy carrier and pricing location","unit":"kW","indices":["t","e","l"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E033","v141-b-g01-E036"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-X004","symbol":"ang_{t,e,l}","meaning":"Voltage angle used in the DC-flow-style network representation; the source also includes this variable for district heating and cooling although its numerical value is irrelevant there.","kind":"operational","domain":"Real-valued; fixed to zero at reference pricing locations L^0 (Eq. 10)","unit":"·","indices":["t","e","l"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E031","v141-b-g01-E034"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-T001","symbol":"q_b","meaning":"Bid quantity in kWh; upper bound on the amount cleared from bid b.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kWh","indices":["b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E024"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-T002","symbol":"Q_r","meaning":"Total quantity for bid dependency r in kWh, used in LE-, GE- and EQ-dependency constraints.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kWh","indices":["r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E026","v141-b-g01-E027","v141-b-g01-E028"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-T003","symbol":"c_{l,k}","meaning":"Transfer capacity limit between adjacent pricing locations l and k.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kW","indices":["l","k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E035"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-T004","symbol":"a_{l,k}","meaning":"Admittance between pricing locations l and k in the source network representation.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kW","indices":["l","k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E033","v141-b-g01-E035"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-T005","symbol":"m_{lo1}","meaning":"Maximum share of district-heating energy that may be supplied from low-temperature pricing location l_lo1.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"dimensionless","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E037","v141-b-g01-E038"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-T006","symbol":"m_{lo2}","meaning":"Maximum share of district-heating energy that may be supplied from both low-temperature pricing locations l_lo1 and l_lo2 together; the source states m_lo2 ≥ m_lo1.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"dimensionless","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E037","v141-b-g01-E039"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted demand bids provide inputs to local market clearing. Scope: Supply-and-demand inputs to the local multi-energy-carrier auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E022"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The requested quantity submitted in a demand bid limits the quantity cleared from that bid: clearing cannot exceed its bid quantity. Scope: The cleared quantity of each demand bid in the local auction.","expression":"0 \\leqslant y_b \\leqslant q_b, \\quad \\forall b \\in B.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E001","v141-b-g01-E024"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted supply bids provide inputs to local market clearing. Scope: Supply-and-demand inputs to the local multi-energy-carrier auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E022"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The offered quantity submitted in a supply bid limits the quantity cleared from that bid: clearing cannot exceed its bid quantity. Scope: The cleared quantity of each supply bid in the local auction.","expression":"0 \\leqslant y_b \\leqslant q_b, \\quad \\forall b \\in B.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E001","v141-b-g01-E024"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The solution of the consumer-and-producer-surplus optimization determines which bids are accepted or rejected in local clearing. Scope: Allocation decisions produced by the local market's surplus-maximizing optimization.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.social_welfare","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E040"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C006","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local market operator operates the clearing function. Scope: Operation of the local market clearing function.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C007","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Receipt of demand submissions forms part of the joint all-bids-received condition under which the operator clears the local market. Scope: The centralized two-sided auction's joint all-bids receipt condition. Condition: All bids for the auction have been received, encompassing both supply and demand submissions.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C008","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Receipt of supply submissions forms part of the joint all-bids-received condition under which the operator clears the local market. Scope: The centralized two-sided auction's joint all-bids receipt condition. Condition: All bids for the auction have been received, encompassing both supply and demand submissions.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C009","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The design clears multiple energy carriers simultaneously through one common optimization. Scope: Common local clearing of multiple energy carriers.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E24"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C010","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The market is cleared once per hour, shortly before each delivery-hour begins. Scope: The paper's rolling-horizon implementation with one-hour delivery periods. Condition: The time-period length is assumed to be 1 h.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C011","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each clearing returns results for the full trading horizon. Results for the upcoming binding hour are final, while results for subsequent advisory hours are updated in later clearings. Scope: Allocation results across the rolling trading horizon.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g03-E01"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C012","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Centralized local clearing decides how to dispatch these assets optimally. Scope: Assets whose flexibility is represented using the model's bid-dependency instruments. Condition: Agents apply bid dependencies to provide asset flexibility to the market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E24"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C013","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Partial clearing of bids is permitted. Scope: Acceptance of bids in the proposed local market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E019"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C014","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The amount cleared from a bid must be nonnegative. Scope: The cleared amount of every bid.","expression":"y_b \\geqslant 0, \\quad \\forall b \\in B.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X001"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E024"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C015","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Net energy injection must equal net outflow at each pricing location, ensuring that total supply equals total demand for each time-period and energy carrier. Scope: Each pricing location, time-period and energy carrier in local clearing.","expression":"inj_{t,e,l} = flo_{t,e,l}, \\quad \\forall t \\in T,\\; e \\in E,\\; l \\in L.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X002","v141-c-R003-X003"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E036"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C016","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Clearing must respect network transfer limitations so that accepted bid combinations do not produce flows beyond local distribution-network capabilities; transfers between adjacent pricing locations are bounded by transfer capacity. Scope: Network-constrained allocations between carrier-specific pricing locations within the local market.","expression":"(ang_{t,e,l} - ang_{t,e,k}) a_{l,k} \\leqslant c_{l,k}, \\quad \\forall t \\in T,\\; e \\in E,\\; l \\in L,\\; k \\in L_l.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X004"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T003","v141-c-R003-T004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g01-E035"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C017","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The same proportion of every bid in the dependency must clear. Scope: Local clearing of bids in the same AND-dependency. Condition: Bids are included in an AND-dependency.","expression":"\\frac{y_{b_i}}{q_{b_i}} = \\frac{y_{b_j}}{q_{b_j}}, \\quad \\forall (b_i,b_j) \\in r, \\; \\forall r \\in R^{AND}.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E025"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C018","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The total accepted quantity from the dependency's bids must not exceed the specified amount. Scope: Local clearing of bids in an LE-dependency. Condition: The dependency type is LE.","expression":"\\sum_{b \\in r} y_b \\leqslant Q_r, \\quad \\forall r \\in R^{LE}.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E018","v141-b-g01-E026"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C019","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The total accepted quantity from the dependency's bids must be at least the specified amount. Scope: Local clearing of bids in a GE-dependency. Condition: The dependency type is GE.","expression":"\\sum_{b \\in r} y_b \\geqslant Q_r, \\quad \\forall r \\in R^{GE}.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E018","v141-b-g01-E027"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C020","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The total accepted quantity from the dependency's bids must equal the specified amount. Scope: Local clearing of bids in an EQ-dependency. Condition: The dependency type is EQ.","expression":"\\sum_{b \\in r} y_b = Q_r, \\quad \\forall r \\in R^{EQ}.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E018","v141-b-g01-E028"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C021","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The sum of the cleared fractions of the dependency's bids must not exceed one. Scope: Local clearing of bids in the same OR-dependency, including partial acceptance. Condition: Bids are included in an OR-dependency.","expression":"\\sum_{b \\in r} \\frac{y_b}{q_b} \\leqslant 1, \\quad \\forall r \\in R^{OR}.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E029"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C022","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"An individual out-of-the-money bid may be accepted only with compensating bids that make its dependency collectively in-the-money. Scope: Acceptance of individual bids connected by AND-dependencies or OR-dependencies. Condition: An individual bid is out-of-the-money and other bids in its dependency compensate for it so that the dependency altogether is in-the-money.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E043"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C023","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"No bids in the OR-dependency clear when the dependency as a whole is unprofitable. Scope: The implemented inequality formulation of an OR-dependency. Condition: The bid dependency as a whole is unprofitable.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E030"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C024","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The proportion of district heat supplied from low-temperature sources must be restricted to ensure that the water reaches a sufficiently high temperature. Scope: District-heating allocations involving low-temperature heat sources. Condition: Heat sources deliver below the target temperature of the district-heating system.","expression":"flo_{t,l_{lo1}} \\leqslant m_{lo1}\\left(flo_{t,l_{lo1}} + flo_{t,l_{lo2}} + \\sum_{k \\in L^{hi}} flo_{t,k}\\right), \\quad \\forall t \\in T; \\qquad flo_{t,l_{lo1}} + flo_{t,l_{lo2}} \\leqslant m_{lo2}\\left(flo_{t,l_{lo1}} + flo_{t,l_{lo2}} + \\sum_{k \\in L^{hi}} flo_{t,k}\\right), \\quad \\forall t \\in T.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X003"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T005","v141-c-R003-T006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E037","v141-b-g01-E038","v141-b-g01-E039"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C025","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"Net energy injection at each pricing location is defined as the total cleared supply-bid quantity minus the total cleared demand-bid quantity for that time-period, energy carrier and pricing location.","expression":"inj_{t,e,l} = \\sum_{b \\in S} y_{b,t,e,l} - \\sum_{b \\in D} y_{b,t,e,l}, \\quad \\forall t \\in T,\\; e \\in E,\\; l \\in L.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X001","v141-c-R003-X002"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E032"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C026","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"Net energy outflow from each pricing location is defined as the sum over adjacent pricing locations of the angle difference multiplied by admittance.","expression":"flo_{t,e,l} = \\sum_{k \\in L_l} \\left[(ang_{t,e,l} - ang_{t,e,k}) a_{l,k}\\right], \\quad \\forall t \\in T,\\; e \\in E,\\; l \\in L.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X003","v141-c-R003-X004"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E033"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C027","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"One pricing location per energy carrier is assigned as a reference location, and its voltage angle is fixed to zero so that voltage angles are uniquely identified.","expression":"ang_{t,e,l} = 0, \\quad \\forall t \\in T,\\; e \\in E,\\; l \\in L^0.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X004"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E034"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E001","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p02-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"M. Brolin and H. Pihl Nomenclature L0 Ll Algebraic symbols vb qb B , b set and index of bids Q D , d","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"B, b set and index of bids; D, d set and index of demand bids, D ⊂ B; S, s set and index of supply bids, S ⊂ B; R, r set and index of bid dependencies; R^X set of bid dependencies of type X, R^X ⊂ R; T, t set and index of time steps; E, e set and index of energy carriers; L, l set and index of pricing locations."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E006","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"the local market and other surrounding energy systems. A retailer uptherefore does not represent a p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The local market clearing function is matching the submitted supply and demand bids, taking into account aspects such as grid constraints. The clearing function is operated by a market operator, which is responsible for the continuous operation of the local market and its supporting functions, and should therefore preferably be financially independent from the owners of the market participants."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E007","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Electrical Power and Energy Systems 118 (2020) 105739 of 4.1. Main ingredients s- se 4.1.1. Centrali","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Like many wholesale electricity markets, the proposed market is based on a centralized two-sided auction format. It is a centralized auction in the sense that all agents submit bids to a central market operator, at a specific time and in accordance with a standardized bid format. Once all bids have been received, the market operator clears the market, meaning that it identifies which bids should be accepted, based on the information contained in the bids. The market operator informs each agent whether or not their bids cleared."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E012","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"4.1.3. Rolling time-horizon a- Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-periodn- len","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-period length is the same for all energy carriers. Energy in different time-periods are traded as different commodities, and agents submit separate bids for separate time-periods. For clarity, we will here assume that the time-period length is 1 h. However, the time-period length could be both longer and shorter."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E013","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"4.1.3. Rolling time-horizon a- Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-periodn- len","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In order to minimize forecast errors, bid submission and market clearing take place as close to the delivery-hour as possible. Therefore, bids are submitted and the market is cleared once per hour, shortly before the beginning of each delivery-hour. However, for the market to be able to accommodate dependencies over longer periods of time, each market clearing also includes a range of future hours. The full range of hours included in a market clearing is referred to as the trading horizon. The first hour in the trading horizon (the upcoming delivery-hour) is referred to as the binding hour, and subsequent hours are referred to as advisory hours. As the names indicate, the market results for the binding hour are final, whereas the results for the advisory hours will be updated in subsequent market clearings."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E018","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a 4. single quantity (in kWh) an","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"AND-dependencies: The bids should be treated by the market as complements that need to be accepted or rejected in tandem. LE-dependencies: The sum of the accepted quantity from the bids should be less than or equal to a certain amount. GE-dependencies: The sum of the accepted quantity from the bids should be greater than or equal to a certain amount. EQ-dependencies: The sum of the accepted quantity from the bids should be exactly equal to a certain amount. OR-dependencies: The bids should be treated by the market as substitutes, such that at most one of the bids can be fully accepted."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E019","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"GE-dependencies: The sum of the accepted quantity from the bids qb • should be greater than or equal","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The suggested market allows for partial clearing of bids, and the dependencies are constructed to be compatible with partial clearing. For bids that are tied together with an AND-dependency, this means that the bids should be cleared in equal proportion: if 70% of one bid clears then 70% of the other bids in the same dependency should also clear. For bids that are tied together with an OR-dependency, it means that the sum of the fraction of bids that clear should not exceed 100%: if 70% of one bid clears then at most 30% of another bid can clear."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E021","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"st th4.1.5. Network constraints The suggested market design takes network transfer limitations expli","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The suggested market design takes network transfer limitations explicitly into account when clearing the market. The purpose of this is to prevent the market from clearing a combination of bids that would lead to energy flows that the local distribution networks cannot handle. This is achieved by subdividing the local market into pricing locations, which are defined such that the most important network constraints can be captured as transfer limits between the different locations. The pricing locations are energy carrier-specific, since the appropriate pricing location definitions may be different for different energy carriers. In case of network congestion, the market prices at the various pricing locations will adjust to reflect the marginal value of energy in every pricing location. Hence, the principle of nodal pricing as presented in e.g. [38] is applied, and extended to incorporate different energy carriers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E022","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Electrical Power and Energy Systems 118 (2020) 105739 re 4.2. Market clearing and pricing re This se","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"This section provides a mathematical description of the market clearing mechanism, including all the main ingredients discussed in Section 4.1. The market clearing is based on mathematical optimization, where the objective is to maximize the sum of consumer and producer surplus. The problem is kept linear, which means that it can be solved efficiently using available linear programming (LP) software. Input to the market clearing problem consists of bids and bid dependencies, and outputs are the cleared bid quantities and market prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E023","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a 4.2.1. Objective and bid dependencies m The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize ","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize consumer and producer surplus, i.e. the difference between the sum of the valuations of all cleared demand bids and the sum of the valuations of all cleared supply bids. The optimization variables are y_b, denoting the amount to clear from each bid. \\max_{y_b} \\left[ \\sum_{b \\in D} v_b \\cdot y_b - \\sum_{b \\in S} v_b \\cdot y_b \\right] \\tag{1}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E024","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a 4.2.1. Objective and bid dependencies m The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize ","equation_id":"(2)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The amount to clear from each bid should be non-negative and cannot exceed the bid quantity: 0 \\leqslant y_b \\leqslant q_b, \\quad \\forall b \\in B. \\tag{2}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E025","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a 4.2.1. Objective and bid dependencies m The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize ","equation_id":"(3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For bids included in an AND-dependency, the same proportion of each bid should clear the market. Therefore, an AND-dependency that includes N bids requires N − 1 equality constraints as follows: \\frac{y_{b_i}}{q_{b_i}} = \\frac{y_{b_j}}{q_{b_j}}, \\quad \\forall (b_i,b_j) \\in r, \\; \\forall r \\in R^{AND}. \\tag{3}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E029","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ds qbi qbj j (3) For each LE-, GE-, and EQ-dependency, there is a constraint ensuringds that the tot","equation_id":"(7)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For each OR-dependency, there is a constraint ensuring that the sum of the fraction of bids that clear is less than or equal to 1, as: \\sum_{b \\in r} \\frac{y_b}{q_b} \\leqslant 1, \\quad \\forall r \\in R^{OR}. \\tag{7}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E030","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ds qbi qbj j (3) For each LE-, GE-, and EQ-dependency, there is a constraint ensuringds that the tot","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The OR-dependency is here formulated using an inequality instead of a strict equality. The reason for this is to ensure that the absolute value of the valuations submitted in the bids are meaningful. With a strict equality, only the relative valuations of the bids within the dependency would influence the market outcome, and a bid could clear the market even if it was out-of-the-money. With an inequality, no bids would clear if the bid dependency as a whole is unprofitable. If a market participant wants to ensure that at least one bid clears, this can still be achieved using high enough bid valuations."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E035","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"(angt , e , l angt , e , k ) al , k ⩽ c l , k , C ∀ t ∈ T , e ∈ E , l ∈ L , k ∈ Ll . (11) al pe Fina","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The amount of energy that can flow between adjacent pricing locations l and k is limited by a transfer capacity limit, which can be expressed as (ang_{t,e,l} - ang_{t,e,k}) a_{l,k} \\leqslant c_{l,k}, \\quad \\forall t \\in T, e \\in E, l \\in L, k \\in L_l. \\tag{11}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E036","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"(angt , e , l angt , e , k ) al , k ⩽ c l , k , C ∀ t ∈ T , e ∈ E , l ∈ L , k ∈ Ll . (11) al pe Fina","equation_id":"(12)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Finally, power balance constraints ensure that net injection equals net outflow in each pricing location (this will also ensure that total supply equals total demand, for each time-period and energy carrier): inj_{t,e,l} = flo_{t,e,l}, \\quad \\forall t \\in T, e \\in E, l \\in L. \\tag{12}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E037","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"(angt , e , l angt , e , k ) al , k ⩽ c l , k , C ∀ t ∈ T , e ∈ E , l ∈ L , k ∈ Ll . (11) al pe Fina","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Concerning DH, additional constraints might be needed to accommodate low-temperature heat sources that delivers heat at temperature below the target temperature of the DH system. In such cases, the proportion of DH supplied from low-temperature sources needs to be restricted to ensure that the water reaches a high enough temperature. As an example, two low-temperature sources are here assumed, but the method can be easily extended to include any number of heat sources. Two low-temperature pricing locations are created accordingly, including only these two supply sources. The locations are denoted l_{lo1} and l_{lo2}, where the supply at l_{lo1} operates at a lower temperature than the supply at l_{lo2}. The remaining high-temperature supply sources are located at a set of pricing locations collectively referred to as L^{hi}. The maximum share of DH energy that can be supplied from l_{lo1} is denoted m_{lo1}, and the maximum share supplied from both low-temperature locations is denoted m_{lo2}, where m_{lo2} \\geqslant m_{lo1}. The low-temperature constraints are therefore nested:"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E040","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"al ( y y), j o- have preferred to trade (they are out-of-the-money). The market clearing prices can ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The solution to the market optimization problem determines which bids should be accepted and which should be rejected. This is done without introducing any price variables into the optimization problem. However, the market operator needs to determine one price for each time-period, energy carrier, and pricing location. In a general microeconomic sense, a price is considered to clear a market if, at that price, the total amount that producers would like to sell equals the total amount that consumers would like to buy. Hence, the market operator needs to find market clearing prices that are compatible with the optimization problem solution so that all accepted bids should be willing to trade (they are in-the-money), and none of the rejected bids would have preferred to trade (they are out-of-the-money)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E043","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Crucially, the shadow prices provide appropriate market clearing prices also when bids are connected","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Crucially, the shadow prices provide appropriate market clearing prices also when bids are connected with AND-dependencies or OR-dependencies. In these cases, an individual bid may be accepted even if it is out-of-the-money, but only if other bids in the same dependency compensate for it, such that the dependency altogether is in-the-money. Further, when network limitations are implemented, the shadow prices for the power balance constraints will differ across pricing locations, and each accepted bid will be in-the-money relative to the price at its pricing location."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E24","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p08-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"6.3. Multiple energy carriers and flexibility instruments","anchor_text":"the ﬁnal settlement amounts. A more detailed comparison between the id alternative settlement approa","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In order to facilitate the integration of different energy carriers, the proposed market design clears multiple energy carriers simultaneously through one common optimization. This increases the possibility to use synergies and thereby an efficient use of resources. The proposed model includes different bid dependency options that the agents can apply in order to provide the market with flexibility, but leaves for the centralized market clearing to decide on how to dispatch such assets in an optimal way. The implemented instruments are based on logical relations between bids, offering a wide range of flexibility options (e.g. load shifts between hours and the shift of energy carrier), but also the possibility to impose restrictions on the independence of operation of equipment coupled to different energy systems (e.g. for heat pumps and CHPs)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p08-c2r2__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"6.2 Rolling horizon and financial settlement","anchor_text":"p ; p y the market clearing function or having a more complex decision making function of the agents","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the proposed market design, each market clearing returns market results for the full trading horizon. However, only the results for the first hour in the horizon, the binding hour, is used for financial settlement."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E002","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p02-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Electrical Power and Energy Systems 118 (2020) 105739 L0 set of reference locations, L0 ⊂ L Ll set o","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"L^0 set of reference locations, L^0 ⊂ L; L^l set of locations connected to pricing location l; v_{b,t,e,l} bid valuation [€/kWh]; q_{b,t,e,l} bid quantity [kWh]; Q_r total quantity for bid dependency [kWh]; y_{b,t,e,l} amount cleared from bid [kWh]; a_{l,k} admittance between locations [kW]; c_{l,k} transfer limit [kW]; inj_{t,e,l} net energy injection [kW]; flo_{t,e,l} net energy outflow [kW]; ang_{t,e,l} voltage angle [·]; λ_{t,e,l} market clearing price [€/kWh]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E026","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ds qbi qbj j (3) For each LE-, GE-, and EQ-dependency, there is a constraint ensuringds that the tot","equation_id":"(4)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For each LE-, GE-, and EQ-dependency, there is a constraint ensuring that the total amount cleared satisfies the total quantity restriction: \\sum_{b \\in r} y_b \\leqslant Q_r, \\quad \\forall r \\in R^{LE}, \\tag{4}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E027","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ds qbi qbj j (3) For each LE-, GE-, and EQ-dependency, there is a constraint ensuringds that the tot","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\sum_{b \\in r} y_b \\geqslant Q_r, \\quad \\forall r \\in R^{GE}, \\tag{5}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E028","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ds qbi qbj j (3) For each LE-, GE-, and EQ-dependency, there is a constraint ensuringds that the tot","equation_id":"(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"and \\sum_{b \\in r} y_b = Q_r, \\quad \\forall r \\in R^{EQ}. \\tag{6}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E031","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"tions and withdrawals at the various pricing locations. The appropriate way to model this depends on","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The network model for the electrical grid is based on a DC power flow model approximating the AC power flows on electricity networks, having the advantage of keeping the optimization problem linear. The district heating and cooling networks are modeled as radial networks, such that there is just one way for energy to flow between any two locations in the network model. This means that the model can be kept relatively simple, since there is no need to formulate equations that model the flow of energy over a meshed grid. In order to keep the optimization problem description as tractable as possible, the variable names and equations from the direct current power flow model is used also for the district heating and district cooling models. For example, a variable named “voltage angle” is included also for the district heating and cooling network locations, although the value for this variable is irrelevant for these networks."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E032","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"culate the net injection of energy at the pricing location, and the total outﬂow of energy from the ","equation_id":"(8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For every time-period, energy carrier and pricing location, we calculate the net injection of energy at the pricing location, and the total outflow of energy from the pricing location to the adjacent pricing locations according to inj_{t,e,l} = \\sum_{b \\in S} y_{b,t,e,l} - \\sum_{b \\in D} y_{b,t,e,l}, \\quad \\forall t \\in T, e \\in E, l \\in L, \\tag{8}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E033","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"culate the net injection of energy at the pricing location, and the total outﬂow of energy from the ","equation_id":"(9)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"flo_{t,e,l} = \\sum_{k \\in L_l} \\left[(ang_{t,e,l} - ang_{t,e,k}) a_{l,k}\\right], \\quad \\forall t \\in T, e \\in E, l \\in L. \\tag{9}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E034","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"culate the net injection of energy at the pricing location, and the total outﬂow of energy from the ","equation_id":"(10)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"One pricing location per energy carrier needs to be assigned as a reference location (or slack location) for the voltage angles to be uniquely identified. ang_{t,e,l} = 0, \\quad \\forall t \\in T, e \\in E, l \\in L^0. \\tag{10}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E038","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Electrical Power and Energy Systems 118 (2020) 105739 cy and llo2, where the supply at llo1 operates","equation_id":"(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"flo_{t,l_{lo1}} \\leqslant m_{lo1} \\left( flo_{t,l_{lo1}} + flo_{t,l_{lo2}} + \\sum_{k \\in L^{hi}} flo_{t,k} \\right), \\quad \\forall t \\in T, \\tag{13}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E039","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"te al and s, flot , llo1 + flot , llo 2 ⩽ mlo 2 (flot , llo1 + flot , llo 2 er ⎞ + ∑ flot , k ⎟ , ∀ ","equation_id":"(14)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"flo_{t,l_{lo1}} + flo_{t,l_{lo2}} \\leqslant m_{lo2} \\left( flo_{t,l_{lo1}} + flo_{t,l_{lo2}} + \\sum_{k \\in L^{hi}} flo_{t,k} \\right), \\quad \\forall t \\in T. \\tag{14}"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E006","quote":"The local market clearing function is matching the submitted supply and demand bids, taking into account aspects such as grid constraints."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E022","quote":"Input to the market clearing problem consists of bids and bid dependencies"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E024","quote":"The amount to clear from each bid should be non-negative and cannot exceed the bid quantity"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E001","quote":"D, d set and index of demand bids, D ⊂ B"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E006","quote":"The local market clearing function is matching the submitted supply and demand bids, taking into account aspects such as grid constraints."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E022","quote":"Input to the market clearing problem consists of bids and bid dependencies"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E024","quote":"The amount to clear from each bid should be non-negative and cannot exceed the bid quantity"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E001","quote":"S, s set and index of supply bids, S ⊂ B"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E040","quote":"The solution to the market optimization problem determines which bids should be accepted and which should be rejected."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E023","quote":"The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize consumer and producer surplus, i.e. the difference between the sum of the valuations of all cleared demand bids and the sum of the valuations of all cleared supply bids."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E006","quote":"The clearing function is operated by a market operator"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E007","quote":"Once all bids have been received, the market operator clears the market"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E006","quote":"The local market clearing function is matching the submitted supply and demand bids"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E007","quote":"Once all bids have been received, the market operator clears the market"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E006","quote":"The local market clearing function is matching the submitted supply and demand bids"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E24","quote":"the proposed market design clears multiple energy carriers simultaneously through one common optimization."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E012","quote":"For clarity, we will here assume that the time-period length is 1 h. However, the time-period length could be both longer and shorter."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E013","quote":"Therefore, bids are submitted and the market is cleared once per hour, shortly before the beginning of each delivery-hour."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","quote":"In the proposed market design, each market clearing returns market results for the full trading horizon."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E013","quote":"The first hour in the trading horizon (the upcoming delivery-hour) is referred to as the binding hour, and subsequent hours are referred to as advisory hours. As the names indicate, the market results for the binding hour are final, whereas the results for the advisory hours will be updated in subsequent market clearings."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E24","quote":"The proposed model includes different bid dependency options that the agents can apply in order to provide the market with flexibility, but leaves for the centralized market clearing to decide on how to dispatch such assets in an optimal way."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E019","quote":"The suggested market allows for partial clearing of bids"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E024","quote":"The amount to clear from each bid should be non-negative"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E036","quote":"Finally, power balance constraints ensure that net injection equals net outflow in each pricing location (this will also ensure that total supply equals total demand, for each time-period and energy carrier)"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E021","quote":"The suggested market design takes network transfer limitations explicitly into account when clearing the market. The purpose of this is to prevent the market from clearing a combination of bids that would lead to energy flows that the local distribution networks cannot handle."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E021","quote":"The pricing locations are energy carrier-specific"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E035","quote":"The amount of energy that can flow between adjacent pricing locations l and k is limited by a transfer capacity limit"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E025","quote":"For bids included in an AND-dependency, the same proportion of each bid should clear the market."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E018","quote":"LE-dependencies: The sum of the accepted quantity from the bids should be less than or equal to a certain amount."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E018","quote":"GE-dependencies: The sum of the accepted quantity from the bids should be greater than or equal to a certain amount."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E018","quote":"EQ-dependencies: The sum of the accepted quantity from the bids should be exactly equal to a certain amount."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E029","quote":"For each OR-dependency, there is a constraint ensuring that the sum of the fraction of bids that clear is less than or equal to 1"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E043","quote":"Crucially, the shadow prices provide appropriate market clearing prices also when bids are connected with AND-dependencies or OR-dependencies. In these cases, an individual bid may be accepted even if it is out-of-the-money, but only if other bids in the same dependency compensate for it, such that the dependency altogether is in-the-money."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E030","quote":"The OR-dependency is here formulated using an inequality instead of a strict equality."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E030","quote":"With an inequality, no bids would clear if the bid dependency as a whole is unprofitable."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E037","quote":"Concerning DH, additional constraints might be needed to accommodate low-temperature heat sources that delivers heat at temperature below the target temperature of the DH system. In such cases, the proportion of DH supplied from low-temperature sources needs to be restricted to ensure that the water reaches a high enough temperature."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"30c6b6991cfd61b1b799d254eb344c70e1cc108413a120f4d632513d6fc80e46","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Formalized the clearing quantity bounds, AND/LE/GE/EQ/OR dependency constraints, network transfer and power-balance constraints, and district-heating low-temperature share constraints from source Eqs. (2)-(14). Procedural/organizational and pricing-interpretation statements without direct formulas remain not_formalized. B evidence is unreviewed under the experimental policy. Source Eq. (11) is transcribed as printed without an absolute value, and Eqs. (13)-(14) are transcribed as printed without an energy-carrier index on flo; these source ambiguities remain for review rather than being repaired here.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-X001","node_ids":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R003-E001","v141-c-R003-E003"],"rationale":"y_b is the cleared quantity produced by local clearing for every bid. The demand and supply bid-quantity bounds are represented by the limit edges from bidding.demand and bidding.supply to clearing.local."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-X002","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Net injection is an auxiliary clearing quantity at pricing locations, defined by the clearing network representation; no dedicated edge exists in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-X003","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Net outflow is an auxiliary clearing quantity at pricing locations, defined by the clearing network representation and used by the transfer and district-heating constraints."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-X004","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Angle is an auxiliary network variable in the clearing model, including the source's formal reuse of voltage angle for thermal networks."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-T001","node_ids":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R003-E001","v141-c-R003-E003"],"rationale":"q_b is the submitted bid quantity that bounds the cleared amount through the demand and supply limit edges into clearing.local."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-T002","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Q_r is the dependency total-quantity parameter applied by clearing to bids in LE, GE and EQ dependencies; no dependency-specific edge exists in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-T003","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"c_{l,k} is a transfer-capacity parameter of the network representation used inside local clearing."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-T004","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"a_{l,k} is an admittance parameter of the source network representation used inside local clearing."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-T005","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"m_lo1 bounds the low-temperature district-heating share in clearing; no separate DH node exists in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-T006","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"m_lo2 bounds the combined low-temperature district-heating share in clearing; no separate DH node exists in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","node_ids":["bidding.demand","clearing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R003-E001"],"rationale":"The demand bid quantity bound is attached to the limit edge from bidding.demand to clearing.local; the source Eq. (2) is universal over B, and it therefore applies in particular to demand bids D."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C004","node_ids":["bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R003-E003"],"rationale":"The supply bid quantity bound is attached to the limit edge from bidding.supply to clearing.local; the source Eq. (2) is universal over B, and it therefore applies in particular to supply bids S."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C014","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Nonnegativity of cleared bid quantities is part of the clearing variable domain and has no dedicated edge in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C015","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The power-balance equality is an internal clearing constraint at each pricing location, time-period and energy carrier."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C016","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The transfer-capacity inequality is an internal network constraint of local clearing."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C017","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The AND-dependency equal-proportion constraint is a clearing constraint on bid quantities; no dependency edge exists in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C018","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The LE-dependency total-quantity upper bound is a clearing constraint on bids in a dependency."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C019","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The GE-dependency total-quantity lower bound is a clearing constraint on bids in a dependency."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C020","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The EQ-dependency total-quantity equality is a clearing constraint on bids in a dependency."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C021","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The OR-dependency fractional-capacity constraint is a clearing constraint on bids in a dependency."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C024","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The nested district-heating low-temperature share constraints are internal clearing constraints on outflows from the specified pricing locations."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C025","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The net-injection definition supports internal clearing network balance and relates cleared bid quantities to pricing-location injection."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C026","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The net-outflow definition supports internal clearing network balance and transfer constraints."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C027","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The reference-angle normalization supports the internal clearing network representation and has no dedicated edge in the frozen graph."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
